THIRD-PARTY / LICENSE NOTICES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is MIT-licensed (see above) with the following exceptions
and external dependencies. If you redistribute the application -- especially
the prebuilt binaries from GitHub Releases -- you must comply with these
licenses for the parts they cover.

1. workers/pixiv.py -- GPL-2.0-only
   This file contains code adapted from gallery-dl
   (https://codeberg.org/mikf/gallery-dl, Copyright 2014-2026 Mike Faehrmann,
   license GPL-2.0-only). It is therefore distributed under the terms of the
   GNU General Public License version 2, not MIT. See the header of that
   file and https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html.

2. gallery-dl tool (external, optional, never bundled) -- GPL-2.0-only
   The Zerochan worker can drive a separately installed copy of gallery-dl
   out-of-process (``python -m gallery_dl``). No gallery-dl code is shipped
   in this repository or inside the prebuilt binaries. At startup (source
   runs only), core/gallery_dl_interop.py (MIT, our own code) may enable the
   ``page-html`` option inside the user's *own installed copy* of
   gallery-dl; frozen builds skip this and use the built-in Zerochan JSON
   API engine instead. gallery-dl remains governed solely by its own
   GPL-2.0-only license: https://codeberg.org/mikf/gallery-dl

3. rule34Py library (external dependency, bundled in binaries) -- GPL-3.0-only
   The Rule34 worker imports the rule34Py package
   (https://pypi.org/project/rule34Py/), which is licensed GPL-3.0-only. It
   is installed via pip (see requirements.txt) and, as an imported library,
   is also contained in the PyInstaller binaries published with GitHub
   Releases. Everyone who receives a binary therefore also receives
   GPL-3.0-covered code; the corresponding source is the upstream rule34Py
   release pinned in requirements.txt plus this repository. See
   https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html.

In short: our own code is MIT; workers/pixiv.py is GPL-2.0-only; gallery-dl
is an external GPL-2.0-only tool that is used but never distributed; and the
rule34Py library (GPL-3.0-only) travels with the dependency install and the
prebuilt binaries. MIT code may be combined into GPL-covered distributions,
so distributing the whole application under the GPL terms for the combined
work satisfies all of the above.
